{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-c-to-d","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-c-to-d","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.md","line":236,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-c-to-d","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-2]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-4]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-lipschitz]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-flow-geodesic]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-uniqueness]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-c-to-d","line":396,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[c $\\Rightarrow$ d: complete metrics have global geodesics]\n\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch7-2-8-c-to-d}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch7-2-2, def:dc-ch7-2-4, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-lipschitz, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-flow-geodesic, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-uniqueness, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound, lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam}\n\n  \\dcref{ch7:2.8}\nLet $M$ be a Riemannian manifold whose distance is the Riemannian distance of\n  $g$ and which is complete as a metric space. Then for every $p\\in M$ and\n  $v\\in T_pM$ there is a geodesic $\\gamma:\\mathbb R\\to M$ with $\\gamma(0)=p$ and\n  $\\gamma'(0)=v$: $M$ is geodesically complete.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch7-2-8-lipschitz, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-flow-geodesic, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-uniqueness, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound, lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam}\n\\sketch If a geodesic stopped at a finite endpoint, the local Lipschitz estimate would make its values a Cauchy family. Metric completeness gives a limit point, and the uniform local flow near that point extends the geodesic past the endpoint. Rescaling handles arbitrary initial velocities.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[c <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Rightarrow $\">$\\Rightarrow $</span> d: complete metrics have global geodesics] <p></p><span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368372d322d382d632d746f2d64\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23def%3Adc-ch7-2-2\">↗ def:dc-ch7-2-2</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23def%3Adc-ch7-2-4\">↗ def:dc-ch7-2-4</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-8-lipschitz\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-8-lipschitz</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-8-flow-geodesic\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-8-flow-geodesic</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-8-uniqueness\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-8-uniqueness</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-6-reparam\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch7:2.8</span></span>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> be a Riemannian manifold whose distance is the Riemannian distance of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g$\">$g$</span> and which is complete as a metric space. Then for every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v\\in T_pM$\">$v\\in T_pM$</span> there is a geodesic <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma :\\mathbb R\\to M$\">$\\gamma :\\mathbb R\\to M$</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (0)=p$\">$\\gamma (0)=p$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma &#x27;(0)=v$\">$\\gamma &#x27;(0)=v$</span>: <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is geodesically complete.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-8-lipschitz\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-8-lipschitz</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-8-flow-geodesic\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-8-flow-geodesic</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-8-uniqueness\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-8-uniqueness</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-6-reparam\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam</a> \\sketch If a geodesic stopped at a finite endpoint, the local Lipschitz estimate would make its values a Cauchy family. Metric completeness gives a limit point, and the uniform local flow near that point extends the geodesic past the endpoint. Rescaling handles arbitrary initial velocities. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-a-to-b","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-2","title":"def:dc-ch7-2-2","label":"def:dc-ch7-2-2"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-4","title":"def:dc-ch7-2-4","label":"def:dc-ch7-2-4"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-lipschitz","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-lipschitz","label":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-lipschitz"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-flow-geodesic","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-flow-geodesic","label":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-flow-geodesic"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-uniqueness","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-uniqueness","label":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-uniqueness"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound","label":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#thm:dc-ch7-2-8","title":"thm:dc-ch7-2-8","label":"thm:dc-ch7-2-8"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#cor:dc-ch7-2-9","title":"cor:dc-ch7-2-9","label":"cor:dc-ch7-2-9"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-c-to-d","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-c-to-d","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[c $\\Rightarrow$ d: complete metrics have global geodesics]\n\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch7-2-8-c-to-d}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch7-2-2, def:dc-ch7-2-4, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-lipschitz, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-flow-geodesic, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-uniqueness, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound, lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam}\n\n  \\dcref{ch7:2.8}\nLet $M$ be a Riemannian manifold whose distance is the Riemannian distance of\n  $g$ and which is complete as a metric space. Then for every $p\\in M$ and\n  $v\\in T_pM$ there is a geodesic $\\gamma:\\mathbb R\\to M$ with $\\gamma(0)=p$ and\n  $\\gamma'(0)=v$: $M$ is geodesically complete.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch7-2-8-lipschitz, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-flow-geodesic, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-uniqueness, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound, lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam}\n\\sketch If a geodesic stopped at a finite endpoint, the local Lipschitz estimate would make its values a Cauchy family. Metric completeness gives a limit point, and the uniform local flow near that point extends the geodesic past the endpoint. Rescaling handles arbitrary initial velocities.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-2","title":"def:dc-ch7-2-2","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-4","title":"def:dc-ch7-2-4","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-lipschitz","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-lipschitz","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-flow-geodesic","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-flow-geodesic","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-uniqueness","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-uniqueness","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}